{
  "about": [
    "MSFP's media part (spec/v0/media.md): what MSFP adds to MSFP Media's fetching as it carries it between servers, its carrier vectors: the scan ticket (media section 4.2). The rest of fetching's cases, and the subtitle and font checks of MSFP Media's video, are MSFP Media's, in https://github.com/msfp-io/msfp-media/blob/main/vectors/v0/fetching.json and https://github.com/msfp-io/msfp-media/blob/main/vectors/v0/video.json. The owning server is fetching's source, the viewer's server its caller. Generated by tools/vectors from the specification's rules.",
    "names: a name, the URL's path after <stream root><ticket>/, under a scan ticket: valid, served; else 404, and reason says why (media section 4.2), as in MSFP Media's fetching.json.",
    "scans: the owning server's answer to a fetch under a scan ticket, MSFP's own, that has already sent sent body bytes (MSFP media section 4.2), for the scanBytes its scan answer states (MSFP playback section 8; absent: none, and the cap is the floor, 4,194,304 bytes, the value the caller counts on; out of 4 MiB to 1 GiB: the floor too): status 206 with its Content-Range, cut short at the cap, or 416 with Content-Range: bytes */<size>."
  ],
